      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-13T13:38:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like all the other places in this CL would support making a build that has both webgpu and webgl support compiled in. I\"m guessing that would be helpful for testing purposes (or for clients that want to use webgpu when it\u0027s available, with a fallback to webgl?). Seems like this \u0027else\u0027 going to prevent that, though?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 197,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "1d665eb3ab3266c29ccbf6a8a22837bbe31d930f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba04eb8f_2cedf94a",
        "filename": "modules/canvaskit/BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 197,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-13T13:58:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s going to be best if we only have our WebGL or our WebGPU backend compiled in at once. The client should be able to do feature detection and get the right version as desired.",
      "parentUuid": "dae9f68a_3f54be0c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 197,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "1d665eb3ab3266c29ccbf6a8a22837bbe31d930f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40ea5c2e_8fda5d63",
        "filename": "modules/canvaskit/BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 197,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-14T21:59:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Kevin, would you mind explaining why you prefer to have one backend compiled in at once? I can think of some nuances in emscripten flags but I don\u0027t fully understand the ramifications.\n\nOne thing that definitely stood out to me is that the way the WASM C++ bindings are structured right now (the code uses a lot of conditional compilation to export certain symbol names) it will be easier to do a first pass that does only one of the backends. Though, I think we could eventually restructure the bindings code to better modularize WebGL vs WebGPU vs CPU-only functions.",
      "parentUuid": "ba04eb8f_2cedf94a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 197,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "1d665eb3ab3266c29ccbf6a8a22837bbe31d930f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6942304e_baefbdb1",
        "filename": "modules/canvaskit/BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 197,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-15T12:02:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The primary concern is codesize - adding more GPU backends to a single build means a larger .wasm blob, which is one of the largest complaints with CK.",
      "parentUuid": "40ea5c2e_8fda5d63",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 197,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "1d665eb3ab3266c29ccbf6a8a22837bbe31d930f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fc18dc6_25cb4d36",
        "filename": "modules/canvaskit/BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 197,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-15T13:27:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right. I think that it should probably be the default that we only build one or the other, but that should be a decision made when building. This particular chunk of code seems to make it a *requirement* that only one is present?",
      "parentUuid": "6942304e_baefbdb1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 197,
        "endChar": 8
      },
